<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#archery">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as archers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Archery is the use of bows to shoot arrows in hunting and warfare. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mounted-archer">Mounted archers</a> were the core of steppe armies such as those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>, and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>, famous for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a>. Foot archers were also important in earlier states, including the Akkadian and Kushite empires, the latter renowned for its bowmen.</p></div>
